package org.mattshoe.mtg.core

internal val storyWeatherlight = StorySection(
    "weatherlight", "Weatherlight Saga",
    "For centuries Urza built a ship, a weapon and a bloodline for one war against Phyrexia, and when the war came it took the ship, the heir and Urza himself.",
    listOf(
        StoryArticle(
            "the-legacy", "The Legacy",
            listOf(
                StoryTab(
                    "tolaria", "Tolaria",
                    listOf(
                        "Centuries after the [Sylex blast](sylex-blast) ended the Brothers' War, [Urza](who/urza) came back to Dominaria a planeswalker with one purpose left. He knew Phyrexia was coming. With the wizard Barrin he founded an academy on Tolaria, a lonely tropical island far out in the western ocean, and he filled it with children, because the Phyrexians never made their sleeper agents in the shape of a child. Barrin taught them magic. Urza set them to work on his war.",
                        "His first plan was the boldest he ever had. He would build a machine that could reach back to the age of the Thran and stop Phyrexia before it began. No living thing could survive the stresses of travelling through time, and Urza's studies showed that only silver passed through them unharmed, so he built a probe of silver in the shape of a man. So that it could think and choose for itself, he set inside it a heartstone that had once belonged to Xantcha, a Phyrexian who had turned against her makers and travelled at his side.",
                        "Urza handed the new golem to a gifted and careless student named [Teferi](who/teferi), who treated it like a toy and called it Arty Shovelhead. An older student, Jhoira, took the golem away from him and taught it properly. She gave it a Thran word for strength as its name. It was [Karn](who/karn), and for a while the island was a good place to be young and clever.",
                        "It did not last. A Phyrexian named Kerrick came to the academy, and in the attack that followed Jhoira was killed. Karn used the time machine to go back and save her. He succeeded, and the machine failed catastrophically. The Tolarian temporal disaster tore the school apart and left the island a broken patchwork of fast time and slow time. Urza escaped with Barrin and a handful of scholars, Karn pulled thirty-three more out of the wreck, and Jhoira was left alone on the ruined island. Teferi was caught in a bubble of slow time, hanging in the air and on fire.",
                        "Ten years passed before Urza, Barrin and Karn came back with a new class of students. They found Jhoira alive, living in a cave on the western shore, and together she and Karn worked out how to free Teferi. The {Tolarian Academy} rose again on an island where an hour in one valley could be a year in the next, and Urza meant to use every one of those hours.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "the-skyship", "The Skyship",
                    listOf(
                        "The time machine had failed, so Urza turned to building. Over the years he made and gathered a collection of artifacts that would be greater than the sum of its parts, a weapon that could kill [Yawgmoth](who/yawgmoth) himself. His people called it the Legacy. A book called the {Thran Tome}, whose pages showed each reader something different, held the plan of how the pieces were meant to fit together.",
                        "The heart of the Legacy was a ship. Its bones were Thran metal, forged in Shiv at the ancient Mana Rig, where Urza had talked the viashino and the goblins into working side by side. Its hull grew from the Weatherseed, the seed of the oldest magnigoth tree in Yavimaya, a gift from the forest's guardian spirit Multani. Urza had to make his peace with that forest before it would give him anything at all.",
                        "The ship still needed power. Urza found it in Serra's Realm, the plane the planeswalker Serra had made long ago, which was failing and riddled with Phyrexian corruption. He offered to move its people to safety. When they refused he invaded, and filled a great powerstone with the realm's white mana as it collapsed. The skyship's maiden voyage was a rescue, carrying thousands of refugees out of a dying world, with Jhoira as its first captain and Karn aboard. Its name was the Weatherlight.",
                        "Jhoira did not stay. She went home to Shiv to run the Mana Rig with Teferi, and Karn missed her so badly that he sank into a depression nothing could lift. Barrin begged Urza to help him. Urza's answer was a cap on the golem's memory, so that Karn could only ever hold twenty years of his life at once. The one thing Karn refused to lose was Jhoira, and every night he held her picture and told himself again that she was his friend.",
                        "So the {Skyship Weatherlight} was finished, the finest thing Urza ever made. It was built for a war that had not started yet, and it had nobody worthy to fly it.",
                    ),
                    quote = StoryQuote("To make peace with the forest, make peace with me.", "Multani, Maro-Sorcerer"),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "bloodlines", "Bloodlines",
                    listOf(
                        "Urza was an artificer, and for a long time he believed that a good enough weapon would be enough. It was not. The Legacy needed a human being to wield it and to lead Dominaria's people when the Phyrexians came, and so Urza set out to make one. He tried breeding generations inside Tolaria's fast time, and the children went mad. He accepted at last that the work had to be done in real time, one marriage and one birth after another.",
                        "The Tolarian Academy turned its whole strength to what became the Bloodline Project. Across Dominaria, families strong in white mana were nudged and steered until the academy all but chose who married whom. Urza took a special interest in the warrior houses of Benalia and Jamuraa, above all the Capashen clan and the line that would one day produce a ship's captain named Sisay. Barrin fell in love with a Tolarian woman named Rayne, who rose to be the academy's chancellor. Only after they were married did he learn that Urza had picked her for him, and that their unborn daughter Hanna was already part of the plan.",
                        "The second phase went further. Urza ordered a whole race of engineered soldiers, the Metathran, and Barrin openly turned against his methods. Some researchers quit rather than take part. One of those who stayed, a man named Gatha, began splicing Phyrexian stock into his subjects, and when he was thrown out he took his work to Keld. Far away, Phyrexia was making a plane of its own as a staging ground for the invasion, and its name was [Rath](rath-made).",
                        "Phyrexia noticed what Urza was doing and struck first. Raiders fell on the sites of the Bloodline Project and killed thousands. The Capashen clan was slaughtered, and so were Sisay's parents. Karn had been given to the Capashens as their guardian, and out of the burning he carried one small boy. The Weatherlight itself had already been handed to a wealthy family in Zhalfir to keep it out of Phyrexian sight. Everything Urza had built now rested on an orphan named Gerrard.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "gerrard", "Gerrard",
                    listOf(
                        "Karn took the boy south to an ally of Urza's, the Jamuraan warlord Sidar Kondo, who adopted him. Gerrard grew up in Kondo's war-clan with a silver golem for a shadow. Kondo's own son Vuel despised the newcomer at first. Over the years the two boys became brothers in everything but blood.",
                        "Phyrexia had not finished with Gerrard. It sent a man from Rath, Starke il-Vec, to work his way into the tribe. When Vuel faced his rite of passage, a climb up a sheer plateau that had to be made alone, Starke poisoned the paint used for his ritual markings. Vuel weakened and fell from the cliff. Gerrard caught him and saved his life, and by saving him made him a failure, because a rite faced with help was a rite failed. The clan cast Vuel out. His own father turned him away.",
                        "Starke found the young man in his despair and fed his grievance until it became hatred. Vuel came to believe Gerrard had stolen his birthright. He took the Legacy artifacts Gerrard kept, disabled Karn, and sold the treasures to pay for an army of raiders, which he led against his own people. Sidar Kondo died in the fighting. Karn went after the stolen Legacy, was tricked into killing an innocent man, and was frozen into a statue by one of the artifacts, the Touchstone. Then Vuel simply vanished.",
                        "Gerrard was not there for any of it. He had gone north to train under Multani in Yavimaya, alongside an elf named Rofellos and a cat warrior named Mirri, who had been cast out by her own kind because her eyes did not match. Mirri loved Gerrard and never told him. He thought of her only as his closest friend, and he once fought a ritual contest so that she would not have to marry a warrior she did not want. When he came back to Jamuraa he found his family's camp destroyed and his foster father dead, and nobody left to tell him why.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "sisays-crew", "Sisay's Crew",
                    listOf(
                        "The Weatherlight had passed to Sisay, a Zhalfirin girl whose parents had been killed by a power she knew only as the Lord of the Wastes. She was taken by slavers, rescued by pirates, and grew up a sailor. When she came into her inheritance she set out to find the scattered pieces of a legend she only half understood, because she had heard that together they could kill the thing that murdered her family. She never knew that the Lord of the Wastes was Yawgmoth. Along the way a young minotaur named Tahngarth fought as her champion and stayed on as her first mate.",
                        "Gerrard, Rofellos and Mirri joined her crew after Gerrard lost a knife-throwing wager to her in a tavern. Aboard were the navigator Hanna, Barrin's daughter, who had left Tolaria to study artifice in New Argive, and her friend Orim, a healer. There was a moody Urborg noble named Crovax and a goblin cabin hand named Squee. For a few years they hunted the Legacy across Dominaria, and Gerrard and Hanna fell in love.",
                        "Then a message came from Crovax's family estate on Urborg, which was under attack by two Phyrexian horrors. The crew came to help and arrived too late to save his family. Rofellos was killed in the fighting, and Crovax turned the battle only by calling down Selenia, the angel bound to an heirloom of his house. Gerrard had seen enough people die for a destiny he never asked for. He walked away from the ship and from Hanna, and Mirri went with him.",
                        "Gerrard became a soldier in Benalia, among the surviving Capashens, and won a name for himself exposing a corrupt commander. Sisay kept hunting. A Rathi fugitive called Starke came to her claiming to have turned against his masters, and he told her where the pieces of the Legacy were. She gathered them, and then she was taken. One day Tahngarth found Gerrard in a Benalish training yard and told him that the captain had been carried off to another plane, to [Rath](rath-stronghold), by the people who had made it.",
                        "Gerrard had no interest in the Legacy. He went anyway, because his friends needed him, and he went knowing almost nothing about where he was going.",
                    ),
                ),
            ),
            listOf(
                StorySource("Set", "Urza's Saga"),
                StorySource("Set", "Urza's Legacy"),
                StorySource("Set", "Urza's Destiny"),
                StorySource("Set", "Weatherlight"),
                StorySource("Novel", "Time Streams, by J. Robert King"),
                StorySource("Novel", "Bloodlines, by Loren L. Coleman"),
                StorySource("Novel", "Rath and Storm, edited by Peter Archer"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Tolaria"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Skyship Weatherlight"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Bloodline Project"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Gerrard Capashen"),
            ),
        ),
        StoryArticle(
            "rath-stronghold", "Rath",
            listOf(
                StoryTab(
                    "predator", "Predator",
                    listOf(
                        "Before the Weatherlight could cross between worlds, somebody had to set the destination into the Thran crystal at the heart of its engine. Hanna asked her estranged father Barrin to come. He refused, and sent instead one of his best apprentices, a young wizard named Ertai, who was brilliant and knew it. The crew collected the rest of its company on the way. Mirri came out of Llanowar. Crovax came out of Urborg, still grieving for his angel. Starke came too, rescued from a warlord who had been sent to hold him, and he told them at last why he had served the Phyrexians. They had his daughter Takara.",
                        "Gerrard also found [Karn](who/karn), still frozen where Sisay had stored him in the ship's hold, and woke him with an instinct for artifice that came to him as heir to the Legacy. Karn woke remembering the innocent man he had killed. He swore never to take another life.",
                        "Rath was a [made plane](rath-made), a world of flowstone and endless storm, and it was waiting for them. The moment the Weatherlight arrived, the evincar's flying warship came for it. The {Predator, Flagship} grappled the smaller ship and boarded her, led by its commander, {Greven il-Vec}. Karn let himself be carried off rather than fight. Tahngarth leapt across to the enemy ship to save him and was taken too. The Legacy artifacts went with them. Gerrard dueled Greven on the deck, took a cut across the face that would scar, and was thrown overboard when a shot from the Predator sent the Weatherlight spinning.",
                        "The Predator flew back to the Stronghold to report that Gerrard was dead. Crippled and leaderless, the Weatherlight came down in the Skyshroud Forest, with Hanna in command and the planeshifting engine broken.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "korvecdal", "Korvecdal",
                    listOf(
                        "Gerrard was not dead. He fell into the forest, fought off the merfolk who found him, and stumbled onto a pilgrimage of the Vec, one of Rath's human tribes. With them was a prophetess, the {Oracle en-Vec}, who told him he was the Korvecdal, the one foretold to unite the Kor, the Vec and the Dal against the evincar who ruled Rath from his Stronghold.",
                        "Hanna and Mirri had gone into the forest to find him, both of them in love with the same man and both of them knowing it. When a shapeshifter caught Mirri, Hanna killed it, and the two women came to an understanding at last. Not long afterwards the elves of Skyshroud took them prisoner and brought them before their lord. {Eladamri, Lord of Leaves} had led a long rebellion against the evincar, and he was in no mood to trust strangers falling out of the sky.",
                        "Gerrard arrived with the Oracle just in time. The prophecy did what no argument could, and the elves freed their captives and called off the attack they had planned on the stranded ship. The crew learned two things from Eladamri's war council. There was an old planar portal nearby, abandoned and leading somewhere unknown. And the rebels were ready to throw everything they had at the Stronghold.",
                        "Gerrard took little interest in being anybody's saviour, but he knew a useful title when he was handed one. Ertai stayed behind to open the portal, and in return for help from Lyna, an emissary of the ghostly Soltari, he agreed to let her people use it too. The rest of the crew flew for the Stronghold while the tribes and the elves attacked it from outside. Starke went quietly with them, worrying about his daughter and trying very hard to stay out of the Oracle's way.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "the-stronghold", "The Stronghold",
                    listOf(
                        "The Weatherlight went into the heart of the fortress by way of the Furnace of Rath and the Death Pits, and the crew went on foot from there. Volrath's Stronghold was a puzzle box of traps and shapeshifters. Inside they found what had been done to their friends. Tahngarth had been strapped beneath a mutating ray to be remade as Greven's new second in command, and he came out bent and changed for life. Karn had been locked in a tumbling room full of goblins, forced to crush them as he fell, a torture designed for a golem who had just sworn never to kill.",
                        "In the dungeons Crovax met the real Selenia, now in the evincar's service. She went for him, and Mirri threw herself in the way and took a terrible wound across the chest. Crovax swung at the angel until she let him strike her. She shattered into hundreds of shards that drove into his flesh, and the curse on his family was fulfilled. He had destroyed what he loved. When Orim saw him back on the ship, his eyes had gone solid yellow and he had fangs. {Crovax the Cursed} had become a vampire.",
                        "Gerrard pushed on with Starke to the Dream Halls at the top of a tower. There the place showed him his own past, Vuel on the cliff, Vuel cast out, Vuel led away by horned figures, and he understood. The evincar of Rath was his brother. After his war against his father, Vuel had been brought to Rath through Starke's portal, given himself to Phyrexia, and been remade into Volrath, a shapeshifter and master of flowstone.",
                        "Volrath met them with Sisay and Takara under his control. Takara blinded her own father with a blade. Gerrard and Tahngarth subdued the two women without killing them, cornered the evincar and cut him down, and the body melted into the shape of one of his experiments. It had been a decoy. Gerrard hacked the thing apart, then gathered up Sisay and ran for the ship.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "exodus", "Exodus",
                    listOf(
                        "On the way out, Karn felt the stolen Legacy nearby and went after it alone. It was in the keeping of the {Sliver Queen}, the mind of a whole hive, and Karn did what nobody else on the ship could have done. He talked to her. He explained that the Legacy was part of him, and she let him take it and go in peace.",
                        "Crovax woke in the sickbay and climbed onto the deck, obeying a voice in his head that told him to wreck the sails. Mirri followed him, still bleeding from Selenia's blade, and caught him at it. They went over the rail together into Volrath's garden. Gerrard was down there too, fighting Greven, and could not reach her. Mirri saw that he would not stop trying, and that if he stayed he would die, as her spirit beast had once foretold. She let Crovax kill her so that Gerrard would save himself. Crovax tumbled down a ravine when the portal closed, and the voice in his head took him to Phyrexia.",
                        "The Weatherlight raced for the portal with the Predator on its tail, and Hanna fired the Skyshaper, a Legacy piece that had only just been fitted. Ertai was hanging from the portal's arch on a rope as they went through, and the ship was going too fast to stop. The portal closed behind them. The Predator slammed into it, and Ertai fell into the wreckage at Greven's feet.",
                        "So the crew escaped Rath with Sisay and most of the Legacy, and left behind Mirri dead, Crovax damned and Ertai a prisoner. They had also, without knowing it, brought Volrath along. He had taken Takara's shape and walked aboard with them, and what he did with that disguise is the story of [Mercadia](mercadia).",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "nemesis", "Nemesis",
                    listOf(
                        "With its evincar gone, Rath fell into chaos. Phyrexia sent Belbe to restore order and choose a successor. She had been made from the body of Eladamri's murdered daughter, an elf princess rebuilt in steel and given no memory of who she had been, and she carried inside her an eye that let [Yawgmoth](who/yawgmoth) watch through her. She had three candidates. Greven commanded the armies. Ertai, the stranded prisoner, was learning to shape flowstone. And Crovax had come back from Phyrexia remade, with oil for blood, no conscience, and a hunger for other people's lives.",
                        "Belbe changed in Rath. She grew curious, then fond of Ertai, then doubtful of everything she served. She blinded the eye inside her and quietly slowed the Stronghold's flowstone production to delay the invasion. Crovax grew stronger by feeding on everyone near him and finally forced the issue with a coup. In the middle of it Volrath came home from Mercadia and challenged Crovax to a duel for the throne.",
                        "Volrath was the better fighter and was winning when he suddenly collapsed. Ertai had tipped the balance with a spell, knowing Crovax would win anyway and would kill everyone watching to heal himself if the fight dragged on. Crovax was the {Ascendant Evincar} now. Belbe sent Eladamri, Takara and the Vec warrior Lin Sivvi to Dominaria through her portal, and Eladamri, still mad with grief at his daughter's corpse walking and talking, killed her with the last drop of the poison that had killed his daughter.",
                        "Crovax made Volrath's death the centrepiece of his coronation. Stripped of his Phyrexian implants, Vuel was injected with liquid flowstone, which Ertai worked inside his veins until it took him apart. The last thing Vuel saw was the sky of Dominaria, his home, as the two planes began to merge. Ertai, with nowhere left to run, knelt to the new evincar and let himself be remade into his creature.",
                    ),
                    quote = StoryQuote("I stepped out. I did not step down.", "Volrath the Fallen"),
                ),
            ),
            listOf(
                StorySource("Set", "Tempest"),
                StorySource("Set", "Stronghold"),
                StorySource("Set", "Exodus"),
                StorySource("Set", "Nemesis"),
                StorySource("Novel", "Rath and Storm, edited by Peter Archer"),
                StorySource("Novel", "Nemesis, by Paul B. Thompson"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Rath and Storm"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Volrath"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Crovax"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Belbe"),
            ),
        ),
        StoryArticle(
            "mercadia", "Mercadia",
            listOf(
                StoryTab(
                    "the-crash", "The Crash",
                    listOf(
                        "The Weatherlight came through the portal broken and fell out of a strange sky onto a farm. A young man named Atalla watched it plough through his family's fields. Most of the crew lived. Some did not, and Gerrard dug their graves himself and would let nobody help until Takara talked him round. While they held a memorial for Mirri and the others, a sudden flood came roaring across the fields carrying warriors in boats, and it swept the ship away with Orim and the wounded still aboard.",
                        "The rest of the crew was surrounded by riders from Mercadia City and marched across the desert to a mountain that stood on its point, with the city perched on its upturned base and a ring of rotting garbage piled around its foot. Mercadia was a place where everything was for sale and nothing was as it seemed. Its streets wound the wrong way. Its fat magistrate was advised by goblins called Kyren, who spoke only in questions and ran the city while pretending to serve it. And for reasons nobody aboard had expected, the Mercadians treated goblins with enormous respect. Squee, the cabin hand, found himself a person of standing.",
                        "Gerrard broke his crew free in the street, using a pacifist golem to dance with a giant and a goblin to tame an enforcer, and turned the brawl into a reputation overnight. Then he walked into the magistrate's tower with Takara and offered a deal. He would train the city's soldiers and lead them against the rebels who had stolen his ship, the Cho-Arrim of the Rushwood forest. In return he would keep the Weatherlight and have it repaired.",
                        "It was a good deal on paper. Gerrard had not yet asked himself who the Cho-Arrim actually were.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "rushwood", "Rushwood",
                    listOf(
                        "Orim found out. The flood that took the ship had been raised by the Cho-Arrim, who believed the Weatherlight was a sign that their god Ramos had returned. Their leader, {Cho-Manno, Revolutionary}, took her in with the wounded. She lived among them for a month, learned their healing magic and their story of Ramos, and fell in love with Cho-Manno. She found among them something she had been looking for all her life.",
                        "Gerrard marched into the Rushwood at the head of a Mercadian regiment and a pack of hired killers called caterans. He ordered that no one fight until he gave the word. The cateran commander ignored him. The living forest rose against the invaders, Gerrard ordered the charge to keep his army from being torn apart in the trees, and when his troops broke out into the Cho-Arrim village the caterans began slaughtering everyone they found. Gerrard tried to stop them and managed only to kill a few of them himself.",
                        "Orim met him in the ruins with the dead around her. Takara reminded him quietly that he had given the order to attack. Then the cateran commander snapped shackles on his wrists. He had been hired by the magistrate for exactly this, and Gerrard was arrested for killing the city's own mercenaries. The Weatherlight was hauled back to Mercadia as the magistrate's prize.",
                        "The crew got itself out with drugged wine and a rain of garbage dumped on the man who was about to execute Gerrard, and it paid for its freedom with a new bargain. The women would sail to the sea city of Saprazzo and bring back the Power Matrix the ship needed, and the men would wait in the magistrate's tower as hostages. Takara kept Gerrard supplied with wine the whole time, and kept talking to him about betrayal.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "bones-of-ramos", "Bones of Ramos",
                    listOf(
                        "At sea, Orim was dragged under by a vast Saprazzan war beast after the crew harpooned it. She used the last of her breath to heal its wound, and it carried her to Saprazzo alive. In that city of merfolk and humans built inside a sunken crater, the crew heard the Saprazzan version of the story of Ramos. Each of Mercadia's outer peoples told it differently. All of them said that Ramos had fallen from the sky carrying their ancestors, that his heart had dropped into the sea, and that his bones lay somewhere in the deep country.",
                        "Orim was framed for a theft and a murder by a Mercadian plot, and cleared when Cho-Manno, who had survived the massacre, appeared and joined minds with her before the grand vizier. The Saprazzans, the Cho-Arrim and the rebels who called themselves Ramosans threw in their lot with the crew. In a storm raised by the rebels, the women broke the men out of the tower, and Gerrard set off with a party to find the Bones of Ramos.",
                        "He found them at Ouramos, a city of dryads in the forest where Ramos fell. In a trance Gerrard learned the truth behind the myth. Ramos was a dragon engine. [Urza](who/urza) had built him to save people from the battlefields of the Brothers' War, and when the [Sylex](sylex-blast) went off he snatched up a school of merfolk, a ship and soldiers from the field and was flung with them through Phyrexia to Mercadia. They came out of the sky burning. His heart, the Power Matrix, fell into the sea, and his crash killed hundreds of thousands. The five crystals called his bones were powerstones. Then {Ramos, Dragon Engine} himself rose out of the ground, a hundred feet tall.",
                        "Ramos agreed to let the stones go. In the night, Takara took them and disappeared.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "takaras-face", "Takara's Face",
                    listOf(
                        "The woman they called Takara had not been Takara since Rath. In front of the magistrate and his Kyren, she had already presented her father Starke as a traitor and cut his throat, and then she melted into the shape of Volrath. The evincar had walked off Rath in her body and spent every day since poisoning Gerrard against his crew. [Karn](who/karn) had begun to suspect it. He had also found, in the city archives, writing much like the Thran script, a hint that Mercadia's ruling families were descended from Thran refugees and had long had dealings with Phyrexia.",
                        "Squee, chasing a bug through the tower, found the proof. Under the city lay a vast hangar full of warships much larger than the Weatherlight and built in the image of the Predator, Phyrexian work, and the Weatherlight itself was down there. Volrath forced Hanna to fit the Bones of Ramos and the Power Matrix into its engine, with Squee slowly strangling as her reason to hurry. Karn turned out to be the key. The {Juju Bubble} he had carried in his chest bound the crystals and the Thran crystal together, and with his arms sunk into the engine he could fly the whole ship with his mind.",
                        "Gerrard fought his way into the hangar and met his brother blade to blade. He remembered from their boyhood that Vuel always favoured his left, attacked to the right and broke through. The Weatherlight came out of the dark with a red beam that disintegrated everything in its path and hauled him aboard. Above, the city rose against its magistrate and the Kyren, and both were killed. Volrath came after the ship in the Recreant, and Gerrard rammed it out of the sky. The evincar fell, cursing, and slipped back to Rath through his portal.",
                        "Then Ramos rose over the city, and the people cried that the Uniter had come. Cho-Manno and Atalla became the new leaders of Mercadia. Orim said goodbye to Cho-Manno, because her place was on the Weatherlight, and Gerrard set a course for home.",
                    ),
                    quote = StoryQuote("Mercadia's masks can no longer hide the truth. Our day has come at last.", "Cho-Manno, Revolutionary"),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "war-in-jamuraa", "War in Jamuraa",
                    listOf(
                        "In the months before the invasion, Dominaria was already at war with itself. The Keldons, a warrior people of the far north, landed on the coast of Jamuraa. The Jamuraan League of City-States threw together a ragged defence and asked for help from the planeswalker [Teferi](who/teferi), once the careless student of Tolaria, and his old teachers Barrin and Rayne came to fight beside him.",
                        "It was not enough to hold back Keld, and the story of that campaign, told in the novel Prophecy, stands almost apart from the saga around it. Its weight falls in the last battle. A Keldon mutant named Greel, who could strike with his mind, killed Rayne. Barrin answered with a fury nobody at Tolaria had ever seen in him. He destroyed the Keldon army, destroyed Greel, and killed the Keldon overlord Latulla.",
                        "Barrin had already lost Hanna to the Weatherlight and its mission. Now he had lost his wife. The Keldon war was settled, and its real cost was paid in a single household. When the skies over Dominaria opened soon afterwards, Barrin went to war with Urza against Phyrexia already grieving, and Urza went on spending the people around him as he always had.",
                        "The Weatherlight came home from Mercadia into those same skies, carrying a crew that had buried friends on two planes and a Legacy almost whole. Gerrard had hardly set foot on Dominaria before the [Invasion](invasion) began.",
                    ),
                ),
            ),
            listOf(
                StorySource("Set", "Mercadian Masques"),
                StorySource("Set", "Prophecy"),
                StorySource("Novel", "Mercadian Masques, by Francis Lebaron"),
                StorySource("Novel", "Prophecy, by Vance Moore"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Mercadian Masques (novel)"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Mercadia"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Barrin"),
            ),
        ),
        StoryArticle(
            "invasion", "Invasion",
            listOf(
                StoryTab(
                    "benalia-falls", "Benalia Falls",
                    listOf(
                        "The Weatherlight was flying over Benalia when the sky split. Portals opened above the country, blacker than night, and a Phyrexian armada came pouring through. [Yawgmoth](who/yawgmoth) had planned this day for millennia. The crew shut down what portals they could and flew to Benalia City to raise the alarm, and the city's officials threw them in jail as troublemakers. In the cell with them was a mysterious blind seer.",
                        "They broke out with the seer, freed prisoners to fight beside them, and killed a great many Phyrexians, and it made almost no difference. Benalia City died to the last person. The Serran angels and Metathran soldiers Urza sent to its defence were cut to pieces. The crew barely survived their first meeting with the invasion's general, {Tsabo Tavoc}, and in that fight Hanna took a wound that would not heal. Orim named it at last. It was the Phyrexian plague.",
                        "All over Dominaria the first stage of the war followed the same pattern. Urza and Barrin woke the Metathran generals, the twins Thaddeus and Agnate, from a slow-time vault on Tolaria and threw their army at the [Caves of Koilos](koilos), where Tavoc had made her headquarters around the only permanent portal between Phyrexia and Dominaria. In Yavimaya the forest and its spirit Multani won outright. In Llanowar, Eladamri, Lin Sivvi and Takara had arrived from Rath to warn the elves, and the elves would not listen until plague bombs began falling. Takara died saving them.",
                        "In Zhalfir, [Teferi](who/teferi) and [Urza](who/urza) closed the portals over the country together. Then Teferi used the released energy to phase his whole homeland out of the world, and part of Shiv with it, rather than see it fight. Urza never forgave him. Meanwhile the blind seer kept appearing aboard the Weatherlight, gave his advice, and vanished again.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "siege-of-koilos", "Siege of Koilos",
                    listOf(
                        "The seer sent the crew wherever the war hung by a thread. They shut down the portals over Llanowar. They made a short jump to Rath, the staging ground of the whole invasion, and brought back live Phyrexians for Orim to study, and from them she made a serum that stopped the plague. The crew was made immune. It came too late for Hanna. They tried to dream her well in the Dream Halls that Eladamri had brought out of Rath, and it failed, because Hanna did not believe it would work.",
                        "At Koilos the siege had stalled. Tavoc captured Thaddeus and vivisected him. The seer sent the Weatherlight there so that Eladamri could take command of the leaderless Metathran, and while the elf fought Agnate in a duel for the right to lead them, Hanna died.",
                        "Barrin learned of it two weeks later, and only because he asked. Urza had known and kept it from him, because he needed Barrin's mind on the defence of Urborg. Barrin dug up his daughter's body, carried it to Tolaria, and cast {Obliterate}, a spell that destroyed the entire island and everything on it.",
                        "Urza gathered planeswalkers to fight beside him in his giant Titan Engines, and the last battle for Koilos began. The crew went into the caves to close the portal and were overwhelmed. Tavoc seized Gerrard through his grief for Hanna. Then a blow to [Karn](who/karn)'s head cracked the cap on his memory, the old memories came flooding back, among them the Phyrexians he had killed to protect Jhoira, and Karn broke his vow. He held Tavoc long enough for Gerrard to break free. Together they wounded her so badly she barely escaped through the portal before Gerrard shut it. The blind seer stepped forward and showed his face. He was Urza, and he and Gerrard destroyed the portal forever.",
                    ),
                    quote = StoryQuote("I might almost pity my enemies—if it wasn't so amusing to watch them die.", "Tsabo Tavoc"),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "the-overlay", "The Overlay",
                    listOf(
                        "Dominaria held a great feast to celebrate. A few days later the sky began to change. Rath, the [made plane](rath-made) Phyrexia had grown for exactly this, began to settle over Dominaria like a second skin, and everything on it came with it. In the area around the Stronghold alone there were more than a thousand portal ships and well over a hundred thousand shock troops. Koilos fell again in a stroke. The war had only just begun.",
                        "The Stronghold came down on Urborg. Crovax, now evincar and in command of the invasion, ate Tsabo Tavoc for her failure. Urza's planeswalkers carried the coalition armies across the world. The Skyshroud forest landed in Keld, where elves and Keldons fought side by side until the dead in the Keldon necropolis rose to fight for Phyrexia. The ancient dragon {Darigaaz, the Igniter} woke the other primeval dragons, and they turned on everyone, Phyrexian and Dominarian alike, until Karn talked sense into him and Darigaaz threw himself into a volcano to break their power.",
                        "On Urborg the coalition fought its way north toward the Stronghold. Tahngarth killed Greven il-Vec in single combat, and Sisay sent the crippled Predator crashing into the fortress. At that moment of victory Ertai stepped out of nowhere, made invisible by his Phyrexian masters, and dragged Gerrard and Squee into the Stronghold.",
                        "There Gerrard met Crovax. The evincar promised him that Yawgmoth could bring Hanna back from the dead, and proved what Phyrexia could do by killing Squee, who came back to life and kept coming back. Gerrard was carried to Phyrexia and knelt before Yawgmoth. Not long afterwards the Weatherlight was smashed out of the sky by the dragon Crosis. Karn climbed out of the wreck carrying the Thran Tome and told the crew he finally knew what to do.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "nine-titans", "Nine Titans",
                    listOf(
                        "Urza had been planning his own counterstroke for a very long time. Eight planeswalkers joined him, among them Freyalise, Lord Windgrace and Tevesh Szat, each in a Titan suit, and the nine of them went to Phyrexia itself to destroy it from within with soul bombs.",
                        "It went well until it didn't. Tevesh Szat betrayed them and killed two of their number. Urza had built a kill rubric into his suit to pour all his power into the bombs if he had to. And then he was inside Phyrexia, a plane he had hated for four thousand years, and he found it beautiful. Yawgmoth spoke to that. Urza destroyed the master soul bomb that was meant to set off all the others, and when his ally Taysir confronted him, Taysir did not survive it.",
                        "Yawgmoth showed him one more thing. Urza's brother Mishra, Yawgmoth said, had been kept and tortured in Phyrexia ever since the Brothers' War. Urza left his brother where he was and went to his knees before the Father of Machines.",
                        "So the two men Dominaria had been built to depend on, the planeswalker who had spent millennia preparing for this war and the heir he had bred to win it, both knelt to Yawgmoth in the same hour. On Dominaria, the crew of the wrecked Weatherlight did not know that yet. They only knew their ship was broken, their captain was gone, and the dead were winning. What came next is the [Apocalypse](apocalypse).",
                    ),
                    quote = StoryQuote("You can build a perfect machine out of imperfect parts.", "Coalition Victory"),
                ),
            ),
            listOf(
                StorySource("Set", "Invasion"),
                StorySource("Set", "Planeshift"),
                StorySource("Novel", "Invasion, by J. Robert King"),
                StorySource("Novel", "Planeshift, by J. Robert King"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Invasion (novel)"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Planeshift (novel)"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Phyrexian Invasion of Dominaria"),
            ),
        ),
        StoryArticle(
            "apocalypse", "Apocalypse",
            listOf(
                StoryTab(
                    "the-arena", "The Arena",
                    listOf(
                        "In Phyrexia, Yawgmoth filled an arena with countless copies of himself and set his two new servants to fight each other. The winner would be granted his heart's desire. [Urza](who/urza) wanted to study artifice at Yawgmoth's side. Gerrard wanted Hanna back. Robbed of his planeswalker's power so deep inside Phyrexia, Urza could not match a warrior bred and trained for this, and Gerrard cut off his head.",
                        "Yawgmoth kept his word in his own way. He made Gerrard ten times stronger and wiser than he had been and sent him a woman who looked exactly like Hanna. Gerrard looked at her and saw a replica. He drove his blade into it. Yawgmoth had hidden his own essence in that copy, sure it was the one place Gerrard would never strike, and in a flinch of pure reflex he flung Gerrard out of Phyrexia altogether. Gerrard was still holding Urza's head.",
                        "He landed in the throne room of the Stronghold. Squee was there, and the two of them cut down the Phyrexian guards together. On Dominaria, meanwhile, Karn was changing. Breaking his vow had shattered the cap on his memory completely, and he had begun to know things he could not possibly know. He merged the wrecked Weatherlight with the Thran Tome, and the ship was reborn as a living, thinking creature.",
                        "Multani, who had lived in the ship's wood, could no longer stay inside something with a mind of its own. He went home to Yavimaya, found nearly every other forest and kingdom on the way had fallen, and decided not to wait his turn. He tore a whole piece of Yavimaya up by the roots and set it down on Urborg, at the Stronghold's door.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "the-stronghold-burns", "The Stronghold Burns",
                    listOf(
                        "Crovax had left his throne to fight the transplanted forest and was driven back by it. When Ertai saw that he could not beat Gerrard alone, he called the evincar home. Under the mountain, a band of dwarves had found the dormant volcano the Stronghold sat in, and they were tunnelling toward its heart to wake it.",
                        "Gerrard and Squee fought Ertai and Crovax in the throne room while the coalition armies broke in through the dwarves' tunnel and the living Weatherlight, which had found Squee on its scanners, came in behind them. Gerrard killed Crovax with an axe. Squee fiddled with the controls of a Phyrexian rejuvenation chamber until it exploded, and {Ertai, the Corrupted} died in the blast. Everyone the crew had lost on Rath was accounted for now, one way or another. They lifted off just before the dwarves flooded the Stronghold with lava.",
                        "Far away, the four planeswalkers left of Urza's nine set off the last soul bomb by hand, and it gutted Phyrexia. It should have been a victory. Then one of them, Commodore Guff, told the others what he had seen. Yawgmoth had already left. After nine thousand years of exile, the Father of Machines was going home.",
                        "He came back to Dominaria as a vast black cloud. Everything it touched died, and everything dead got up again to fight for him, down to the soil itself.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "the-death-cloud", "The Death Cloud",
                    listOf(
                        "[Yawgmoth](who/yawgmoth) spread across Dominaria killing as he went. On Urborg the Weatherlight dropped off its passengers to fight, kept only its crew aboard, and watched him come with no idea how to stop him. Then Urza's head spoke. Decapitation was not enough to kill a planeswalker, and Gerrard had been carrying him all this time.",
                        "Urza's plan was to open the Weatherlight's Power Matrix and release Serra's Realm onto Dominaria, which would destroy half the world to save the other half. Karn had a better idea. There was a moon in the sky, the Null Moon, that had been soaking up white mana ever since it was put in orbit nine thousand years before. The ship planeshifted to it, drank in its power, and came back to fire it at Yawgmoth.",
                        "The war went on below without them. Bo Levar, one of the last planeswalkers, discovered that Commodore Guff kept a library that recorded the Multiverse and had already written down Yawgmoth's victory. He argued his friend out of it, and Guff struck the dark destiny out of his book just before the death cloud swallowed him. Bo Levar gave his own life to keep an artists' colony out of Phyrexian hands. Eladamri, Lin Sivvi and their army jumped together from a great treefolk rather than become Yawgmoth's dead.",
                        "The Weatherlight fired its Legacy weapon. Yawgmoth tried to flee back to Phyrexia through the Stronghold portal and found it buried in lava. He turned and fought the blast, overcame it, and became enormous tentacles that seized the ship. The Weatherlight's mind died under the strain of channelling the weapon. Everything Urza had built over all those centuries had been fired, and Yawgmoth was still there.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "the-legacy-weapon", "The Legacy Weapon",
                    listOf(
                        "There was one piece left, and it was Urza. His eyes were the Mightstone and the Weakstone, the two halves of the powerstone he and his brother had split in the caves of [Koilos](koilos) four thousand years before. He asked Gerrard to take them out of his head and set them into two sockets in [Karn](who/karn)'s chest.",
                        "Gerrard did it, and the Legacy was complete. A radiant light poured out of the golem and kept spreading, and it took in every part of the Legacy as it grew, Urza and Gerrard and Karn first. The crew leapt from the ship just before the light swallowed the Weatherlight too. Tahngarth's axe carried the energy into one blow against the tentacles holding the ship, and white mana broke over the whole world and hunted down Yawgmoth's essence wherever it touched him.",
                        "Nobody who survived could say exactly what had happened. They knew only that Yawgmoth was gone and that every Phyrexian on Dominaria went suddenly slack, struck senseless by the death of its god. All over the plane the last survivors walked up to the invaders and took them apart with ease.",
                        "Gerrard Capashen and Urza were dead. The Weatherlight sank off the coast of Urborg. The invasion that Yawgmoth had prepared for nine thousand years had been undone by a ship, a golem and a man Urza had bred for the purpose, and it had cost each of them everything.",
                    ),
                    quote = StoryQuote("In a single blinding flash, Yawgmoth was obliterated, and Urza could finally rest.", "Legacy Weapon"),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "a-silver-planeswalker", "A Silver Planeswalker",
                    listOf(
                        "A year later, survivors came from all over Dominaria to a ceremony on Urborg. Freyalise raised a monument to the fallen on the ground where Crovax's family estate had stood. Afterwards Squee and Tahngarth joined Sisay on a new ship. Orim said she had other travel plans.",
                        "Then Karn appeared beside her. He was not the golem they had known. He had become a planeswalker, the first artificial being ever to carry a spark, and he told them he held the whole Legacy inside him, Urza and Gerrard included. The spark had come out of Urza's powerstone eyes, which had carried within them the essence of the ancient Thran artificer Glacian. After a short and joyful reunion, Karn took Orim to Mercadia, where she had decided to marry Cho-Manno. Sisay, Squee and Tahngarth flew off on their own adventures in their new ship, which they named the Victory.",
                        "The saga that had started with two brothers and a stone in a cave ended with a silver golem who could walk between worlds. Karn had been built as a tool and broken more than once. Now he was free, with no master and no war. Centuries later, among the angels and clerics of Serra's church, Gerrard was still honoured as a martyr.",
                        "Karn did not stay on Dominaria. He went out into the Multiverse and decided to build a world of his own, perfect and silver, called [Argentum](argentum). He took something with him that he did not know he was carrying.",
                    ),
                ),
            ),
            listOf(
                StorySource("Set", "Apocalypse"),
                StorySource("Novel", "Apocalypse, by J. Robert King"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Apocalypse (novel)"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Karn"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Gerrard Capashen"),
            ),
        ),
    ),
)
